Delete a secret (DELETE /v1/vault/secrets/{name}).

Every binding of it stops resolving. A sandbox whose policy still names it does
not silently lose the header: the egress proxy refuses those requests rather
than forward them without the credential.

While the organization's network settings or a template's network policy have a
rule that names the secret, the delete is refused, and the error lists the rules:
without the secret, every sandbox created under them would be refused. Remove the
rules first, or pass --remove-rules to remove them with the secret. New sandboxes
then call those hosts without the credential.

Usage:
  anona-compute vault delete <name> [flags]

Aliases:
  delete, rm

Flags:
  -h, --help           help for delete
      --remove-rules   also remove the network rules that name this secret

Global Flags:
      --api-key string             API key (env ANONA_COMPUTE_API_KEY, ANONA_API_KEY, E2B_API_KEY)
      --api-url string             API URL (env ANONA_COMPUTE_API_URL, E2B_API_URL; default https://api.<E2B_DOMAIN>)
      --json                       JSON output on stdout (same as -o json)
  -o, --output string              output format: text or json (default "text")
      --profile string             config profile to use (env ANONA_COMPUTE_PROFILE; default "default")
      --request-timeout duration   timeout for each non-streaming request, 0 = none (create, pause, resume and fork: 3m0s unless set; streams and uploads are never cut off) (default 1m0s)
  -v, --verbose                    verbose output on stderr
